They say that praying for food is like begging for forgivance.

Generally, it's a bad idea to pray for food unless you've absolutely exhausted
all other resources.  "All other resources?" you ask.  Yup.  Disgusting as it
may seem, try munching on the corpses of some of the dinners--er, monsters 
that you kill.  Also, there are several kinds of food meals in the game:  food
rations, eggs, tins, C- & K-rations, lembas wafers, and probably some others
that I can't think of off-hand.

A note of warning:  Not all corpses are OK to eat.  Some, like kobolds and
bees, are poisonous.  Others, like puddings and blobs, can be acidic.  (Won't
kill you, but will do a little HP damage.)  And never eat a corpse that's
gotten old.  (BTW, it takes a lot less time for undead corpses to rot than
for other corpses.)  Also, there are many other corpses that when eaten, will
do something to you, sometimes good (i.e. giving an intrinsic) or sometimes
bad (i.e. stunning or confusing you).
